 Every write triggers `generator.generate()` which atomically replaces the JSON
 files. ETag in the manifest body is the source of truth for client sync.

+## National KTEL coach platform
+
+KTEL is isolated from the rail database:
+
+```text
+ktel.db (ingestion, review, provenance)
+    -> publication compiler
+ktel-public.db (read-only public rows)
+    -> FastAPI coach queries
+out/ktel/manifest.json + immutable release-addressed JSON packs
+    -> nginx and offline clients
+```
+
+Bootstrap and publish:
+
+```bash
+export SYRMOS_KTEL_DB_PATH="$PWD/db/ktel.db"
+export SYRMOS_KTEL_PUBLIC_DB_PATH="$PWD/db/ktel-public.db"
+python -m scripts.ktel_pipeline seed
+python -m scripts.ktel_pipeline publish
+python -m syrmos_admin.generator
+```
+
+Public coach endpoints:
+
+| Path | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `/api/v1/coaches/manifest` | Release ID and immutable pack hashes |
+| `/api/v1/coaches/operators` | All 62 official intercity operators |
+| `/api/v1/coaches/coverage` | National and per-operator coverage truth |
+| `/api/v1/coaches/sources` | Provenance, rights, and retention policies |
+| `/api/v1/coaches/stops` | Reviewed published coach stops |
+| `/api/v1/coaches/routes` | Reviewed journey patterns |
+| `/api/v1/coaches/routes/{patternId}` | Ordered stops and reviewed geometry |
+| `/api/v1/coaches/journeys` | Date-specific published journeys |
+
+TicketWeb reads are scheduled ingestion only. They never run from public request
+traffic. Live access requires explicit terms approval and credentials injected
+outside the repository. See `ktel.env.example` and
+`docs/KTEL_NATIONAL_PLATFORM.md`.
+
